{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-classical-involution","title":"prop:hodge-star-classical-involution","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":4230,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:hodge-star-classical-involution","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-graded]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-involution]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:wedge-covectors-sign]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:hodge-star-congr-smul]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:blockswap-eq-rotate]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:hodge-star-classical-involution","line":7156,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[The Classical Hodge Involution]\n\\label{prop:hodge-star-classical-involution}\n\n\\uses{prop:hodge-star-graded, prop:hodge-star-involution, lem:wedge-covectors-sign, lem:hodge-star-congr-smul, lem:blockswap-eq-rotate}\n\n\n\n\nFor an oriented $n$-dimensional inner product space and a $k$-covector,\n\\[\n{*}{*}\\omega=(-1)^{k(n-k)}\\omega.\n\\]\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch The second classical block order differs from the mirrored order by the block-swap rotation, whose sign is $(-1)^{k(n-k)}$. Combine this comparison with Proposition \\ref{prop:hodge-star-involution}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[The Classical Hodge Involution] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a686f6467652d737461722d636c6173736963616c2d696e766f6c7574696f6e\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahodge-star-graded\">↗ prop:hodge-star-graded</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahodge-star-involution\">↗ prop:hodge-star-involution</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Awedge-covectors-sign\">↗ lem:wedge-covectors-sign</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahodge-star-congr-smul\">↗ lem:hodge-star-congr-smul</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ablockswap-eq-rotate\">↗ lem:blockswap-eq-rotate</a> <p></p>For an oriented <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-dimensional inner product space and a <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$k$\">$k$</span>-covector, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  {*}{*}\\omega =(-1)^{k(n-k)}\\omega .  \\]\">\\[  {*}{*}\\omega =(-1)^{k(n-k)}\\omega .  \\]</span>  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch The second classical block order differs from the mirrored order by the block-swap rotation, whose sign is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(-1)^{k(n-k)}$\">$(-1)^{k(n-k)}$</span>. Combine this comparison with Proposition <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahodge-star-involution\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-involution\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-70726f703a686f6467652d737461722d696e766f6c7574696f6e\">17</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:blockswap-eq-rotate","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-operator","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-graded","title":"prop:hodge-star-graded","label":"prop:hodge-star-graded"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-involution","title":"prop:hodge-star-involution","label":"prop:hodge-star-involution"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:wedge-covectors-sign","title":"lem:wedge-covectors-sign","label":"lem:wedge-covectors-sign"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:hodge-star-congr-smul","title":"lem:hodge-star-congr-smul","label":"lem:hodge-star-congr-smul"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:blockswap-eq-rotate","title":"lem:blockswap-eq-rotate","label":"lem:blockswap-eq-rotate"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-operator","title":"prop:hodge-star-operator","label":"prop:hodge-star-operator"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-two-involution","title":"prop:hodge-star-two-involution","label":"prop:hodge-star-two-involution"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prob:hodge-star-operator","title":"prob:hodge-star-operator","label":"prob:hodge-star-operator"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-classical-involution","title":"prop:hodge-star-classical-involution","tex":"\\begin{proposition}[The Classical Hodge Involution]\n\\label{prop:hodge-star-classical-involution}\n\n\\uses{prop:hodge-star-graded, prop:hodge-star-involution, lem:wedge-covectors-sign, lem:hodge-star-congr-smul, lem:blockswap-eq-rotate}\n\n\n\n\nFor an oriented $n$-dimensional inner product space and a $k$-covector,\n\\[\n{*}{*}\\omega=(-1)^{k(n-k)}\\omega.\n\\]\n\\end{proposition}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch The second classical block order differs from the mirrored order by the block-swap rotation, whose sign is $(-1)^{k(n-k)}$. Combine this comparison with Proposition \\ref{prop:hodge-star-involution}.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-graded","title":"prop:hodge-star-graded","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:hodge-star-involution","title":"prop:hodge-star-involution","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:wedge-covectors-sign","title":"lem:wedge-covectors-sign","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:hodge-star-congr-smul","title":"lem:hodge-star-congr-smul","description":""},{"node":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:blockswap-eq-rotate","title":"lem:blockswap-eq-rotate","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}